From 61c490348fc3287030db5ed713bf517d60c7848f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:50:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: keep Windows awake for Claude Code in VS Code and dev
 containers

VS Code: Insomnia's hook was a plain command line, which Claude Code runs
through PowerShell when Git Bash isn't installed (common with the VS Code
extension) - a parse error there, so no hook ever ran. Hooks are now written
in exec form (cmd.exe /d /c <launcher>, Claude Code 2.1.139+), independent of
the shell.

The Stop hook has been reported missing in the VS Code extension, so sessions
no longer depend on it: hooks act on the event name, open tool calls are
tracked by tool_use_id (a running build stays awake up to 30 min while
claude.exe lives), and an open turn alone is trusted only after the session
has fired Stop once. Notification no longer re-arms the grace after a turn.

Dev containers: Insomnia runs a loopback bridge (127.0.0.1:47391, reached as
host.docker.internal). The new claude-code-stay-awake Dev Container Feature
installs a POSIX hook via Claude Code's managed-settings drop-in that posts
each event and sends a heartbeat while a turn is open, standing in for the
process check Windows can't do inside a container.

Shared session rules live in session-store.js (atomic writes for every
writer); npm test covers the decision table, the bridge and the container
hook. Verified on Linux with a real Claude Code 2.1.293 binary against a mock
API; not yet run on Windows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
